@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `ind-a-tests-fixtures`
IMPORT `g2-second-schedule`
IMPORT `g2-conditions`

-- STATUS, added by the fleet lead on 2026-10-14 (the comments below were written by the independent author and describe the state when it wrote them):
-- these 6 assertions FAILED against the modules as first written (G2 sent a holder of the certificate of the grade sought to the ungraded row).
-- G2 repaired that (fork FS10) and all 6 now PASS, so this file is a regression test: check.sh expects 0 failures here.

-- ind-a-tests-disagree.l4: assertions that FAIL against the encoding and that ind-a believes are the encoding's
-- fault.  Expected values were decided from the sources before the encoding was opened
-- (work/ind-a/expectations.md); they are left failing on purpose.  EXPECTED TO FAIL: 6 assertions.
--
-- D1 (SCH2-A1a, SCH2-B1a, SCH2-C1).  Second Schedule, item 1 of each Part: column A "without prior training or
-- experience", column B "training of up to 350 / 480 / 720 hours CONFERRING a final certificate in refrigeration
-- and air conditioning of grade 1 / 2 / 3 from the Training Division" (gazette pp. 201, 202, 203).  An applicant who
-- completed that course holds that certificate and has met item 1; s.6(a)(4)(a) ("he holds a final certificate")
-- says the same.  The encoding instead classifies the graded certificate of the grade sought under the ungraded
-- row of the same Part (A.3, B.5, C.6: "a final certificate in refrigeration and air-conditioning studies from the
-- Training Division"), so it demands a further course (50, 50 and 200 hours) that confers a LESSER, ungraded
-- certificate, and refuses the grant without it.
-- Stated assumptions for every grant question: adult Israeli citizen and resident, clean record, programme
-- approved by the Registrar (s.19(b)), no foreign qualification, the fee paid; no training done beyond the course
-- whose certificate is held.

§ `ind-a helpers`

GIVEN application IS AN Application
GIVETH A LIST OF NUMBER
`ind-a items that apply` application MEANS
    map (GIVEN item YIELD item's `the item number`) (`training required for the licence sought` application `ind-a commencement day`)

GIVEN application IS AN Application
      `training done` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`ind-a must grant` application `training done` MEANS
    `the Registrar must grant the licence` application `ind-a commencement day` FALSE `training done` TRUE FALSE TRUE

GIVEN certificates IS A LIST OF Certificate
      kind IS A `Licence kind`
GIVETH AN Application
`ind-a holder of` certificates `seeking` kind MEANS
    `ind-a application` (`ind-a applicant holding` certificates) kind (YMD 2026 3 1)

§ `D1: the certificate of the grade sought, conferred by the item 1 course`

-- SCH2-A1a: grade 1 certificate, grade 1 sought.  Encoding: item A.3 applies (50 hours more); grant refused.
#ASSERT `ind-a must grant` (`ind-a holder of` (LIST `a Training Division certificate of grade 1`) `seeking` `grade 1 licence`) FALSE
#ASSERT NOT elem 3 (`ind-a items that apply` (`ind-a holder of` (LIST `a Training Division certificate of grade 1`) `seeking` `grade 1 licence`))
-- SCH2-B1a: grade 2 certificate, grade 2 sought.  Encoding: item B.5 applies (50 hours more); grant refused.
#ASSERT `ind-a must grant` (`ind-a holder of` (LIST `a Training Division certificate of grade 2`) `seeking` `grade 2 licence`) FALSE
#ASSERT NOT elem 5 (`ind-a items that apply` (`ind-a holder of` (LIST `a Training Division certificate of grade 2`) `seeking` `grade 2 licence`))
-- SCH2-C1: grade 3 certificate (the 720-hour course), grade 3 sought.  Encoding: item C.6 applies (200 hours more).
#ASSERT `ind-a must grant` (`ind-a holder of` (LIST `a Training Division certificate of grade 3`) `seeking` `grade 3 licence`) FALSE
#ASSERT NOT elem 6 (`ind-a items that apply` (`ind-a holder of` (LIST `a Training Division certificate of grade 3`) `seeking` `grade 3 licence`))
